    {
      "name": "Fishhooked",
      "actions": null,
      "traits": [],
      "description": "<p>While it has persistent bleed damage from the fisher's fishing line Strike, a creature has a fishhook embedded in it. The creature can't move farther away from the fisher (though it can move laterally). The fisher can reel the creature in as a single action with the attack and manipulate trait, attempting an athletics|against:fortitude check against the creature's Fortitude DC. On a success, the creature takes 2d4 Slashing Damage damage and is pulled 10 feet closer to the fisher (double the damage and distance on a critical success).</p>",
